\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces The theorem, drawn. Blades: negativity windows of the second knife (levels $6,8,11$), every curve exact; cyan: the shore; diamond: the string at $D=23$. This paper proves no blade of any level, at any $\lambda $, ever reaches the shore --- closest approach $2.17$ dimensions.}}{4}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:knives}{{2}{4}{The theorem, drawn. Blades: negativity windows of the second knife (levels $6,8,11$), every curve exact; cyan: the shore; diamond: the string at $D=23$. This paper proves no blade of any level, at any $\lambda $, ever reaches the shore --- closest approach $2.17$ dimensions}{figure.2}{}}
